    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d21">

                <pb facs="0122" n="20" sameAs="frus:frus1933v01/pg20"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4/1734: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Chairman of the American Delegation</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-03-01T19:00:00+01:00">March 1, 1933—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 1—2 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>547. Our 542, February 24, 9 p.m. Yada, Japanese Minister at Berne, acting chief
                    of Japanese disarmament delegation, just called to inform us that he had been to
                    see Henderson, President of the Conference, and informed him that he had
                    received instructions from the Japanese Government that the Japanese delegation
                    would continue to participate in the work of the Disarmament Conference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
